### Sample requests for the Stage API (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client).
### Start the app first: ./gradlew bootRun   (or: docker compose --profile app up --build)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### List every stage, sorted by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages

### Get one stage by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/1

### Unknown id -> 404 problem detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/999999

### Search: empty filter matches all 109 stages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/search
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Search: "classic competitive" -> 30 stages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ledgeCount": { "min": 2, "max": 2 },
  "features": {
    "walkOffs": false,
    "wallInfinite": false,
    "random": false,
    "water": false,
    "symmetry": true,
    "transform": false,
    "ice": false,
    "hurtBox": false
  }
}

### Search: containment. Stages whose left blast zone stays within -240..-200 -> 43 stages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blastZones": { "left": { "min": -240, "max": -200 } }
}

### Search: open-ended bound. Stages at least 900 wide -> Great Cave Offensive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stageWidth": { "min": 900 }
}

### Invalid request: min > max -> 400 problem detail with an "errors" array
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stages/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stageWidth": { "min": 200, "max": 100 }
}
